   "message": "The diff changes plugin code under plugins/ (hooks, types and userConfig in plugin.json, tests, MOD.md), deletes the specclaw-mod plugin, and edits marketplace.json. No version is bumped in any plugin.json, .codex-plugin/plugin.json or marketplace.json plugins[] entry. The specclaw-mod entry carried 0.8.5, and the diff leaves the remaining plugins on whatever version they had. Bump every plugins/*/.claude-plugin/plugin.json, every plugins/*/.codex-plugin/plugin.json and every plugins[] entry in .claude-plugin/marketplace.json to the same new version.",
   "original_severity": "major",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "R1",
   "scenario": "Users on specclaw 0.8.5 who update get the bundled mod and a changed gate default (block to warn) under the same version number. Marketplace caches keyed on version may never offer the update, so the old specclaw-mod plugin and the new bundled mod can end up running together.",
   "severity": "major"
  }
